  "Wall top pinned (roof.eavesPinM) to the parapet line (12.6 m: dak_min 12.4 Van Spilbergenstraat to 12.96 Jan Maijenbuurt): 3DBAG b3_h_dak_min reads it on most pands, while the median roof height (b3_h_dak_50p, used for flat roofs) reads the rooftop additions (dakopbouwen) on many and would make them five storeys; the additions are not modelled.",
  "Brick: Mercatorstraat sunlit 2020-05, upper wall #bd8776 (lit) to #8f6758 (lower, shaded): drawn #a8735f; its ground storey #605452 to #716562: drawn #6a5a55. Van Spilbergenstraat (overcast only) #615048 scaled by the Mercator overcast/sunlit ratio: drawn #84695e. Shackleton yellow overcast #746640 scaled: drawn #bcaa78.",
  "Kit gaps: the canted top-storey bays of some James Cookstraat and Mercatorstraat pands, the downpipes, the brick corbels and the rooftop boxes are not modelled; those pands keep the plain front.",
  "Held: balcony rows, shops, corner pands, the 13.4 m deep white-glazed ground-floor block in Jan Maijenbuurt."
